You can make a component skip re-rendering when its props have not changed by using `memo` for functional components or by extending `PureComponent` for class components. 

For functional components, wrap your component in `memo`:

```js
const MemoizedComponent = memo(SomeComponent);
```

For class components, extend `PureComponent`:

```js
class MyComponent extends PureComponent {
  // component logic
}
```

Both approaches ensure that the component will not re-render as long as its props (and state for `PureComponent`) remain unchanged [1][3].

